          "paragraph": 1,
          "fragments": [
            {
              "scan": "s113",
              "printed_page": "42",
              "text": "True and firm and established and everlasting and upright and faithful and pleasant and precious and delightful and glorious and awe-inspiring and powerful and ordered and favoured and good and comely is this word for us for ever and ever. In truth He is the God of the world, our King, the Rock of Jacob, the shield of our salvation. From generation",
              "page_start": false
            },
            {
              "scan": "s115",
              "printed_page": "43",
              "text": "to generation does He endure and His Name endures, His throne is firmly founded and His realm and His faithfulness endure for ever. And His words are living and eternal, faithful and delightful always and in all eternity for our fathers and for us, for our children and our coming generations and all the generations of the seed of Israel Thy servants.",
              "page_start": true
            }
          ],
          "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:emet_veyatziv/emet"
        },
        {
          "paragraph": 2,
          "fragments": [
            {
              "scan": "s115",
              "printed_page": "43",
              "text": "For the first and the last it is a good and everlasting word, truth and faithfulness, a statute that never passes away. It is truth that Thou, O Lord, art our God and the God of our fathers, our King, the King of our fathers, our Redeemer, the Redeemer of our fathers, our Creator, the Rock of our salvation, our deliverer and rescuer, that is Thy Name since eternity, there is no God except Thee.",
              "page_start": false
            }
          ],
          "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:emet_veyatziv/al_harishonim"
        },
        {
          "paragraph": 3,
          "fragments": [
            {
              "scan": "s115",
              "printed_page": "43",
              "text": "The aid of our fathers hast Thou ever been, shield and helper of their children after them in every generation. In the heights of the world is Thy dwelling and Thy judgments and Thy love extend to the ends of the earth. Fortunate the man, who listens to Thy commandments and takes Thy Torah and Thy word to heart. In truth Thou art the Lord for Thy people and a strong King to promote their cause. In truth Thou art the first and Thou art the last and except for Thee we have no King, Redeemer or helper. From Egypt has Thou redeemed us, O Lord our God, and from the house of slaves hast Thou freed us. All their first born hast Thou slain and Thy first born redeemed, divided the Sea of Reeds, drowned the arrogant and led those dear to Thee through to safety.",
              "page_start": false
            }
          ],
          "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:emet_veyatziv/ezrat"
        },
        {
          "paragraph": 3,
          "fragments": [
            {
              "scan": "s115",
              "printed_page": "43",
              "text": "Then the waters covered their enemies, not one of them remained.",
              "page_start": false
            }
          ],
          "source_reference": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/106/11",
